# The delivery gate's checks, pinned against makesensedigital/engineering-handbook@v3.7.1.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `test-gate.mjs` — the gate's own two-direction test — cannot run in a
# repository that adopted the standard after its code existed: it builds its known-good fixture by
# copying the repository root and editing the TEMPLATE's placeholders out of it
# (engineering-handbook#55). So the claim that these checks are known to work rests on them matching
# the release where that test passes, and this file makes the gate verify it on every run.
#
# FIVE OF THE SEVEN ARE BYTE-IDENTICAL TO v3.7.1. Two are not, and saying so is the whole point:
#
#   lib.mjs — ONE TOKEN added to `walk()`'s skip list: `.gate-baseline.json`. Without it the
#   ratchet's own baseline is read as site content, its `check|file` keys are read as file
#   references, and every run manufactures a finding whose next baseline key is longer. It does not
#   converge.                                                         engineering-handbook#54
#   upstream digest: db440c871c4c34a92903d698f611e5a3785e8adfbae604f7955712c2e6fd39d6
#
#   check-assets.mjs — ONE TOKEN added to the reference scan's extension list: `css`. A stylesheet
#   is the most common place to reference a font or a background image, and it was the one file type
#   the scan did not read: ten self-hosted woff2 files, correctly referenced, all reported as
#   orphans — while §26 actively recommends self-hosting.            engineering-handbook#59
#   upstream digest: ed724bf540b0bd561cceb9e133d5333b1a2980948dbb7d06dad934170cfbdb3d
#
# Both were found by running the gate rather than by reading it. Debt #5 carries the consequence:
# neither change is covered by a test, and any FURTHER edit fails this check by design. The fix at
# that point is to vendor the pristine template into `scripts/fixtures/landing/` and make
# `test-gate.mjs` run for real — not to re-record the digest.
